<div class="bt-list"><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1">Categories</a> &gt; <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1019">sciences</a> &gt; <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=291">earth sciences</a></div>
<div class="row">
<div class="this-term col-sm-12">
  <div class="pref-label">geochemistry</div>
  <div class="scope-note">Study of the distribution of chemical elements and natural compounds on the earth and in the atmosphere and the chemical processes that affect the earth.</div>
  <div class="non-pref">This category is also used for <span class="uf">chemistry (Earth sciences)</span> and  with <a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=700">maps and atlases</a> for <span class="uf">geochemical anomaly maps</span></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="row mb-4">
<div class="col-sm-12">
  <div class="col-sm-8"><b>Subtopics</b><br/><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1078" title="Branch of chemistry concerned with the elements and compounds that make up soils. Includes chemical processes involving soils.">soil chemistry</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1298" title="Branch of chemistry that deals with the elements and compounds in water.">water chemistry</a><br/>
</div>
  <div class="col-sm-4"><b>See also</b><br/><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=69" title="Technique used to identify chemicals based on the measurement of the spectra produced by atoms and molecules with absorption of electromagnetic radiation.">atomic absorption analysis</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=93" title="The cycling of chemical constituents through a biological system.">biogeochemical cycling</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=141" title="The circulation of carbon in the biosphere, atmosphere, and hydrosphere through a series of processes that include photosynthesis, consumption, and respiration.">carbon cycling</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=142" title="Experimental determination of the proportion of a given stable carbon isotope (C12 or C13) in a sample.">carbon isotope analysis</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=153" title="Chemical techniques used to identify the composition of substances.">chemical analysis</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=158" title="Analytical techniques used to separate or partition the components of a gaseous or liquid mixture by differences in absorption rates during flow around or over surface absorbents such as columns of silica, filter papers, or gels.">chromatography</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=288" title="The structural and compositional changes that the earth has undergone from its formation. Use for discussions of the whole earth (or large sections of it) instead of regional studies.">earth history</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=426" title="Chromatographic technique used to separate or partition the components of a mixture.  Solid and liquid samples are vaporized and passed through a column containing a liquid that differentially absorbs the  molecules.">gas chromatography</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=435" title="Processes affecting the amount, distribution, or structure of chemical elements in air, water, soil, rocks, and minerals.">geochemical processes</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=609" title="Experimental determination of the proportion of a given isotope (or isotopes) in a sample.">isotopic analysis</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=654" title="Analytical technique using mass spectrometry to measure the different isotopic forms of low mass (light) elements such as oxygen, hydrogen, carbon, nitrogen and sulfur that occur in samples.">light stable isotope analysis</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=662" title="Chromatographic technique to separate or partition the components of a mixture in which samples are liquid and passed through a column.">liquid chromatography</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=711" title="Instrumental technique to separate and identify molecules.  Gaseous ions are formed, with or without fragmentation.  Their mass/charge ratios and relative electrical abundance are then measured or the spectra are recorded.">mass spectroscopy</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=727" title="Process by which rocks are altered in composition and texture by extreme heat, high pressure, or the action of chemicals.">metamorphism (geological)</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=783" title="Sensitive laboratory technique for both qualitative and quantitative analysis of elements in samples.  Target nuclei are bombarded with neutron beams to start nuclear reactions which emit characteristic gamma ray radiations.">neutron activation analysis</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=855" title="Experimental determination of the proportion of a given stable oxygen isotope in a sample.">oxygen isotope analysis</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=872" title="Analytical technique using a concentrated beam of charged subatomic particles.">particle-beam spectroscopy</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1191" title="Mass spectrometric measurement of the decay of the radioactive isotope of hydrogen in water samples as a means of dating and investigating changes in water.">tritium analysis</a><br/>
</div>
</div>
